 ## Background
-Scaffold-GS was introduced by Tao Lu, Mulin Yu, Linning Xu, Yuanbo Xiangli, Limin Wang, Dahua Lin, and Bo Dai from Shanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory, The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Nanjing University, and Cornell University [S2]. It was published in CVPR 2024 (arXiv:2312.00109v1, Nov 2023) [S2]. The method addresses the limitations of vanilla 3D-GS, such as free drifting of Gaussians and lack of structural constraints, by introducing a hierarchical representation anchored to a sparse grid derived from SfM points [S2].
+Scaffold-GS was introduced by Tao Lu, Mulin Yu, Linning Xu, Yuanbo Xiangli, Limin Wang, Dahua Lin, and Bo Dai from Shanghai Artificial Intelligence Laboratory, The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Nanjing University, and Cornell University [S2]. The paper "Scaffold-GS: Structured 3D Gaussians for View-Adaptive Rendering" was published in CVPR 2024 (arXiv:2312.00109v1, Nov 30, 2023) [S2]. It builds on the 3D-GS framework [Parent] to address the lack of structural constraints and view-dependent robustness in vanilla Gaussian splatting [S2].
 
